SDL2 video driver behaviour on RISC OS.

- with -d driver=1, a memory report every 10 seconds (!Run sends stderr to
  OpenTTDlog; OpenTTD$Debug in !Run turns it on);
- -v sdl:windowed / sdl:fullscreen, so !Run can choose;
- switching full screen recreates the window (the RISC OS SDL driver can't
  switch an existing window);
- the pointer never "leaves" in full screen;
- drawing on the game thread is off by default (-v sdl:threads turns it on);
- RiscOsKeepDesktopAlive(): lets the Wimp poll (SDL_PumpEvents, main thread,
  at most every 50 ms) while files are read before the main loop runs, so
  the desktop doesn't freeze during loading. Called by patch 13;
- the main loop waits for the next tick with SDL_Delay instead of
  SleepTillNextTick(): that uses std::this_thread::sleep_for, which ends in
  UnixLib's nanosleep and spins in a desktop task, so the game took all the
  processor between frames. SDL_Delay waits in Wimp_PollIdle in a desktop
  window (whole centiseconds; the rest in steps of at most 4 ms).

For OpenTTD 14.1. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-openttd.

